# Draft knowledge entry: Boost CMake unversioned shared libraries still need DT_SONAME on OHOS
id: DRAFT-boost-cmake-unversioned-dt-soname-on-ohos
trigger_tool: cmake|conan|readelf|shadow-ci
phase: build|package|ci-quality-gate
error_signature: "L5a: libboost_.*\\.so 缺少 DT_SONAME|L5_RESULT=fail: soname_gate_failed|BOOST_INSTALL_NO_VERSIONED_LIBS"

severity: 3
category: boost|cmake|elf|soname|ohos
match_keywords: BoostInstall.cmake, DT_SONAME, SONAME, BOOST_INSTALL_NO_VERSIONED_LIBS, target_link_options, TARGET_FILE_NAME, L5a

title: Boost CMake unversioned OHOS shared libraries must keep per-target DT_SONAME
root_cause: >
  Suppressing Boost CMake's versioned shared-library install behavior by gating the VERSION block
  also removes the target metadata that normally makes CMake emit a shared-library SONAME. The
  package can build and the consumer test can link, but the CI L5 quality gate rejects the ELF
  files because downstream linkers cannot address them by SONAME.
affected_scope: >
  Boost CMake-based shared-library Conan recipes on HarmonyOS PC when versioned libboost_*.so.*
  outputs or symlink entries are intentionally suppressed for the package layout.
verification_cmd: |
  CI_PACKAGES="archives/b/boost/1.90.0.2.1" CI_BRANCH="feat/boost-1.90.0.2.1" CI_PR_NUMBER="6712" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh
  readelf -d "$(conan cache path boost/1.90.0.2.1:* 2>/dev/null | head -1)"/lib/libboost_python312.so | rg SONAME

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: add-unversioned-soname-link-option
rec_description: >
  Keep BOOST_INSTALL_NO_VERSIONED_LIBS for OHOS package layout, but add a per-target linker option
  in BoostInstall.cmake before the VERSION block is gated. Use the target's generated file name so
  each shared library receives a matching unversioned SONAME such as libboost_python312.so.
rec_command: |
  if(TYPE STREQUAL "SHARED_LIBRARY" AND BOOST_INSTALL_NO_VERSIONED_LIBS)
    if(CMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_SONAME_CXX_FLAG)
      target_link_options(${LIB} PRIVATE "${CMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_SONAME_CXX_FLAG}$<TARGET_FILE_NAME:${LIB}>")
    else()
      target_link_options(${LIB} PRIVATE "-Wl,-soname,$<TARGET_FILE_NAME:${LIB}>")
    endif()
  endif()
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: boost-install-target-link-option

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: repair-before-signing-only-if-link-option-unavailable
fallback_description: >
  If the Boost CMake target cannot be patched, inspect whether a toolchain-provided ELF editor is
  available and patch SONAME before binary signing. Prefer source-level target link options because
  they match CMake metadata and avoid post-package mutation.
fallback_command: |
  command -v patchelf || command -v llvm-objcopy
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: package-stage-soname-diagnosis

forbid_1_pattern: "disable L5|ignore soname_gate_failed|treat conan create pass as enough"
forbid_1_reason: The package can still fail official CI after build/test succeeds if L5 quality metadata is absent.
forbid_1_consequence: Downstream consumers may receive ELF files with unstable loader/linker addressing.
forbid_2_pattern: "set target VERSION again without checking install layout"
forbid_2_reason: Re-enabling VERSION can reintroduce versioned libboost_*.so.* files or symlink-style install entries on OHOS/HMDFS.
forbid_2_consequence: The original package-layout problem can return while fixing SONAME.

principles: elf-metadata-quality-gate, unversioned-package-layout, target-scoped-link-options
causes:
caused_by: DRAFT-boost-cmake-hmdfs-versioned-soname-links
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of: eigenpy-3.13.0

